# Instructions

For ONLY state.checks.{{ name }}, is the existing proposed ownership acceptable after checking this source's printed role in its full current-page and neighboring context?

Locate this exact source by source_order in local_raw_evidence.target_page. proposed_ownership and OCR stream labels are the decisions to evaluate, not authoritative answers. A previous role suspicion is not proof. Use the source's complete original text, geometry, actual note records/reference marks, adjacent illustrations and nearest genuine reading context. Do not approve a mistaken source role merely because its internal definition/index has been made consistent; consistency does not make body text into a note.

Main reading includes narrative, headings, quotations, separately retained illustration text/labels/credits, instructions, bibliography and autonomous chapter-end commentary. Real detached footnotes and their unmarked continuation belong to citation, even if they are grammatical or long. A standalone illustration caption does not become a detached footnote from its small type or explanatory genre. A quotation or explanation within a real marked note does not become main text merely because it is a complete readable sentence. Follow the concrete printed relationship, not superficial prose style.

Folio numbers, running headers and printing-only continuation directions belong to ignored. Ordinary numeric/formula content is not a folio. An OCR stream may mix body and notes; neither that label nor current ownership establishes truth. Do not discard a mixed source wholesale or invent absent OCR or separators. If an unmatched definition is clearly a note, absence of a surviving body reference is not a role error. An empty/unknown reference is not permission to call every explanatory passage a footnote.

This is an affirmative proof of THIS source's proposed ownership, not another search for faults. Require locatable positive evidence of the proposed printed role and check any concrete conflicting role evidence. A consistent internal definition, a plausible genre, or the absence of a demonstrated contradiction is not affirmative evidence. Unknown or conflicting evidence does not establish this proof. A low proof score alone does not establish an error; it only declines to overrule an independently established role fault.

Its paragraph boundary or reference-index defect is a different proposition. Another source's error and an independent mistake on a neighboring page do not falsify this source's role.

# True

Positive, locatable evidence establishes this source's proposed ownership in its actual printed context, after addressing concrete contrary role evidence. This is affirmative support for that ownership, not merely insufficient evidence to reject it.

# False

The proposed ownership contradicts the printed role, or no adequate affirmative evidence establishes it. Uncertainty, an internally consistent index, or a plausible alternative is insufficient to prove that the current role is correct.
